Cab Driver Website: JSON Content, System Design, Security and Google Maps
1. Architecture
Browser (Next.js, mobile-first)
   │
   ├── Static content  ← /content/*.json (edited by the driver or developer)
   │
   ├── Google Maps JS API (browser)      → map display, Places Autocomplete
   │      key restricted by HTTP referrer
   │
   └── /api/* routes (server only)
          ├── /api/distance  → Google Routes API (computeRoutes)  [server key]
          ├── /api/booking   → validate → save (Google Sheet / DB) → notify driver
          └── /api/track     → optional analytics events

Why this split: autocomplete and the map run in the browser with a referrer-restricted key. Distance and fare run on the server with a separate IP-restricted key, so no one can tamper with prices or steal the key.

