4. Responsive design rules
Item	Rule
Approach	Mobile-first; breakpoints at 640, 768, 1024 and 1280px
Layout	Single column on mobile, 2 columns on tablet, 3 to 4 on desktop (CSS Grid)
Tap targets	At least 48x48px; buttons are full width on mobile
Sticky bar	Fixed bottom Call and WhatsApp bar below 768px; floating WhatsApp button above
Typography	clamp() for headings; body at least 16px so iOS doesn’t zoom on inputs
Images	next/image, WebP or AVIF, lazy loading, explicit width and height to avoid layout shift
Map	Fixed height of 300px on mobile and 450px on desktop; touch-action handled by the Maps SDK
Performance	Load Maps script only when the calculator scrolls into view; target LCP under 2.5s
Languages	EN and HI toggle driven by the _hi keys in the JSON
Accessibility	Alt text, visible focus states, AA contrast, labels on every input
Testing	Check at 360, 390, 768, 1024 and 1440px, plus a slow 3G throttle in DevTools
