5. Security checklist

API keys

 Two separate keys (browser and server), both restricted as described above
 Server key never prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_; .env.local in .gitignore
 Daily quota cap and budget alerts set in Google Cloud

Forms and API

 Validate everything on the server with Zod; never trust client-side checks alone
 Indian mobile regex: /^[6-9]\d{9}$/
 Rate limit /api/distance and /api/booking (use Upstash Redis in production)
 Spam protection: honeypot field plus Cloudflare Turnstile or reCAPTCHA on the booking form
 Sanitise text fields; never render user input as raw HTML (avoids XSS)
 The server calculates fares; ignore any fare sent from the client

